---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ActorLab from "../components/ActorLab.astro";
import Playground from "../components/Playground.astro";
import LivePlayground from "../components/LivePlayground.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Identity playground — Janitor"
  description="Try Janitor locally with example data, or opt in to a real browser identity demo with cached Jev evaluation and a shared call budget."
>
  <main id="main" class="container standalone-lab">
    <div class="page-breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Janitor</a>
      <span>/</span>Playground
    </div>
    <h1>Try Janitor in your browser</h1>
    <p class="playground-intro">
      Try a real visitor ID with your browser, or explore the local examples
      below. The live demo starts only when you choose to share your signals.
    </p>
    <LivePlayground />
    <Playground />
    <ActorLab />
    <div class="experiment-note">
      <h2>What the local examples show</h2>
      <p>
        The two example labs run <code>@janitor/core</code> in your browser
        against made-up browser history and example login records. It does not
        use a real cookie, collect browser signals, call Jev, or send
        observations to a server. The same matching and delegation logic powers
        the library.
      </p>
      <p>
        The example shows scores so you can see how matching works. Production
        HTTP responses keep scores private by default. Identity confidence is an
        experimental matching score. It is not authentication or proof that two
        people are the same person.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/validation/">
        Testing and limitations ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
